"DATA","BH105","0.00","0.20","ROADBASE with gravel: 40mm dia. minus gravels.","N","GRAVEL","",""
"DATA","BH105","0.20","2.60","ZONE 1B/4: Sandy Clayey GRAVEL: fine to coarse grained, angular, light brown, highly to moderately weathered sandstone fragments, some gravels can be broken by finger pressure but generally low to medium strength, gravel content estimated at 60-70%, fines are low plasticity.","N","GRAVEL","",""
"DATA","BH105","2.60","6.10","ZONE 1 CORE: Silty CLAY with trace sands and gravels: medium to high plasticity, orange brown/grey and red, very stiff to hard, moist (Wc < Wp). Gravel fraction is fine to coarse grained consisting of rounded, low strength gravels of red sandstone (possibly oxidised) and light brown, moderately weathered fragments of sandstones of low to medium strength. Gravel fraction estimated at less than 5%. 4.1m: Cobble of medium-high strength sandstone.","N","CLAY","",""
"DATA","BH105","6.10","9.00","6.1m: Lense of gravels and cobbles to 100mm consisting of angular high strength sandstone fragments, slightly weathered, light brown and grey with some sand. Potential cobbles broken up by drilling. 6.3m: Becoming light brown, orange brown and grey, very stiff. 6.75 - 6.95m: Lense of gravel, fine to coarse grained, angular, light brown sandstone, highly to moderately weathered, (cobble pulverised by drilling). 7m: Layer of light brown and red brown, grey material is lower plasticity sandy silt/silty sand, trace of fine oxide red gravels, gravels are highly to moderately weathered. Moist to dry (Wc << Wp) very stiff to hard.","N","SAND","",""
"DATA","BH105","9.00","10.00","9m: Layer of red, grey, orange brown very stiff to hard, moist. core highly broken up by drilling in run 9.0 to 10.5m. 9.2m: Inclined surface in core could be pulled apart by hand. Inclined at 45 degrees. Surface slightly polished and striated in dip direction. The surface is coated with higher plasticity, grey silty clay.","N","CLAY","",""

